# Local environment
#
# ⚠ Everything an operator is told to change lives here or in one of the files
# below, and NOTHING they are told to change is tracked. A tracked file an
# operator has edited is a file the next release can collide with, and until
# 06.09 it was a file that stopped `deploy/rcq-update.sh` outright.
docker-compose.override.yml
deploy/decoy.local/
deploy/Caddyfile.local
.env
.env.local
.env.production
*.env

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/

# Local databases
rcq.db
rcq.db-shm
rcq.db-wal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
# ⚠ Every SQLite file, not just the server's own. The local test scripts each
# leave one behind (test_uin_hold.db and friends), and on 2026-09-03 a `git add
# -A` in a DOCS commit carried three of them into this public repository as
# binary blobs. They held only synthetic rows, but a test artefact in a
# reference implementation reads as something a self-hoster is meant to keep.
*.db

# Uploads (per-deployment data, never committed)
media/
news_media/
evidence/

# IDE / editor
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store

# Logs
*.log

# Apple Push key — never check this in
*.p8

# The island's own certificate (fingerprint mode). The key IS the island's
# identity to every user, and a rotation moves the old pair aside under
# whatever name (island.key.old, a dated copy): everything in certs/ stays
# out, and only the .gitkeep that holds the directory for the mount is in.
certs/*
!certs/.gitkeep
